  "rationale": "Loop over j (N/16=2) outer and i (M/16=3) inner so both B tiles for column block j stay resident in scratchpad rows 16-47 across all three m-tiles, loading each of the 4 B tiles exactly once (4 mvins). The single remaining scratchpad tile slot (row 0) forces 2 A-tile loads per output tile (12 A mvins), giving the minimum feasible DMA input of 16 tiles x 256 = 4096 bytes: holding 2 A tiles instead would leave only 1 B slot and force 12 B loads (4608 bytes), and 2A+2B residency (64 rows) exceeds the 48-row scratchpad. Each output tile does an overwrite compute for k=0 then an accumulate compute for k=1 (out_addr bit 30), followed immediately by mvout since the 16-row accumulator holds only one tile. K=32 gives 32*16384 <= 2147483647; all reductions are in increasing k order via sequential compute pairs. Total expanded commands: 51."
